,\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What should I avoid when choosing a name?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Avoid names that sound like commands (Kit/sit, Bo/no), names too similar to family members, names with negative associations, and names you'd feel uncomfortable shouting in public. Also avoid names that are so common your pet might respond to someone else's call at the park.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Should I pick a name before bringing my pet home?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Having a shortlist is great, but avoid finalizing before meeting your companion. The name that seems perfect on paper might not match the reality of your pet's personality. Arrive with options but stay flexible.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How important is name length for pets?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"One to two syllables is ideal for recognition, but consistency matters more than length. Pets learn whatever name you use regularly. If you love a three-syllable name, it will work fine — your pet will likely respond to the first syllable or a natural nickname anyway.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12\\\",\\